      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(edit): fuzzy edit rewrites unrelated lines across the whole file",
        "body": "Closes #89994\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users editing a file with the edit tool would see unrelated lines silently rewritten when fuzzy matching was used. Trailing whitespace was stripped, smart quotes / en-dashes / special spaces were normalized, and other formatting was changed on lines that were not part of the edit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe edit tool's fuzzy match previously switched the entire file content into a normalized workspace whenever any edit needed fuzzy matching, then wrote that normalized content back to disk. Now fuzzy matching is used only to locate `oldText`; the replacement is applied to the corresponding original-content span, so the rest of the file is preserved exactly.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now rely on the edit tool to change only the requested region. Unrelated whitespace, Unicode punctuation, and line endings outside the edited span remain unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added regression test `does not normalize unrelated lines when a real edit uses fuzzy matching` in `src/agents/sessions/tools/edit.test.ts`.\n- Running the new regression test passes.\n- `oxfmt --check` and `oxlint` pass on the changed files.\n- Full `edit.test.ts` suite: 38/40 tests pass; the 2 failures are the pre-existing Windows path issue in `renders previews through custom edit operations` (unrelated to this change).\n",
